WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.033
Context precision.

2
00:00:02.333 --> 00:00:04.286
Retrieval returned five chunks.

3
00:00:04.286 --> 00:00:06.177
How many were actually useful?

4
00:00:06.177 --> 00:00:08.067
That is what this metric asks.

5
00:00:09.267 --> 00:00:13.567
Context precision asks: of the chunks retrieved, how many were relevant?

6
00:00:13.867 --> 00:00:17.367
It is the signal to noise ratio of your retrieval stage.

7
00:00:17.667 --> 00:00:23.833
RAGAS makes it rank aware, so relevant chunks near the top score better than the same chunks buried at the bottom.

8
00:00:25.033 --> 00:00:27.633
Let's label the top five chunks for one query.

9
00:00:27.933 --> 00:00:30.333
Chunks one, two, and four are relevant.

10
00:00:30.633 --> 00:00:32.593
Chunks three and five are noise.

11
00:00:32.593 --> 00:00:36.267
Three out of five gives a plain precision of zero point six.

12
00:00:37.467 --> 00:00:39.033
Here is the math in Python.

13
00:00:39.333 --> 00:00:42.067
Plain precision is just the relevant fraction.

14
00:00:42.367 --> 00:00:48.133
The rank aware version averages the precision at each relevant position, so early hits count more.

15
00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:51.867
Plain gives point six, and rank aware gives point nine two.

16
00:00:53.067 --> 00:00:54.600
Why does this matter so much?

17
00:00:54.900 --> 00:00:57.700
Irrelevant chunks are not just wasted tokens.

18
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:04.173
Every off-topic paragraph is raw material for the model to weave into a confident, wrong answer.

19
00:01:04.173 --> 00:01:07.067
If faithfulness drops, check precision first.

20
00:01:08.267 --> 00:01:11.600
On Mission Control, precision reads a dismal point four.

21
00:01:11.900 --> 00:01:13.861
Eyeballing the chunks shows why.

22
00:01:13.861 --> 00:01:22.500
Every NASA report opens with the same export control notice, and it was embedded like everything else, so it looks close to almost any query.

23
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:27.167
Filter boilerplate at ingest, and precision climbs to point six two.

24
00:01:27.167 --> 00:01:32.433
Add a cross encoder reranker over the top fifty, and it reaches point eight three.

25
00:01:33.633 --> 00:01:34.361
Let's recap.

26
00:01:34.361 --> 00:01:37.633
Precision is the relevant share of what you retrieved.

27
00:01:37.933 --> 00:01:40.133
Rank aware scoring rewards early hits.

28
00:01:40.433 --> 00:01:42.833
Low precision invites hallucination.

29
00:01:43.133 --> 00:01:46.167
Fix it with ingest filters and a reranker.

30
00:01:46.167 --> 00:01:47.900
Next up: context recall.
